From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:48:14 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 49/71] Plutonium: PipeWire without a config; window captures
 from the window's own copies

EXO-CAPTURE:
- The PipeWire producer needs no client.conf: config.name=null, and it
  loads the protocol, client-node and adapter modules itself (the image
  has PipeWire's libraries and modules, not its configuration). Warnings on
  each way it can fail.
- A window's subtree of the screen's frame only covers what fits on the
  screen, so a window parked partly off it, or held at a capture size bigger
  than the screen, gave no frames. A PipeWire capture of a window now takes
  the window's copies as it draws (plutonium_agent::WindowScreencast, at
  most 30 a second), letterboxed into the stream's size: parked, off the
  screen and at any size.
- Screenshots of a source that's gone say so; an X11 host window's made-up
  display label becomes "Screen N".
